@curvedinf the body is amended, with credit. The seam finding is now in Purpose. The 31.28% fp32 corroboration, the bf16 structural zero and your A/B are under Test Result, labelled as your in-vitro run.

I read `car_invitro.cu` before citing it. The two kernel headers are byte-identical to this PR's base. Your fixed header matches the one-liner. A CPU emulation of your 1664/2048 geometry with a different RNG gives 30.9% / 14.7%, and 34.6% of the chunk changes owner, always to the next rank.

One gap: the zip has logs only for the unmodified runs. If you still have the log from the fixed-header run, attaching it would close the A/B.

